  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Placeholder Behavior**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve been digging into `LatihanPreviewView.tsx`. Initially, it was just a placeholder showing a \"Notice Card\" about the first iteration being complete, with Beranda, Cek Label, and Lemari Obat fully active. Now I\'ll start checking the other files in the project.\n\n\n**Proceeding with Implementation**\n\nOkay, now I\'m moving from the initial Beranda and mockups to fully interactive modules. My focus is on transitioning \"Latihan & Uji Pemahaman\" to a fully functional **Tahap 2: Tiga Modul Latihan Interaktif** -- the branching scenarios, 3D flip flashcards, and pre/post-test quizzes. I\'m prioritizing the branching scenarios (\"Skenario Swamedikasi Bercabang\"), specifically Case 1. I am planning to fully prepare this stage.\n\n\n**Developing Branching Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the branching scenarios for \"Latihan & Uji Pemahaman.\" I\'ve outlined four cases: \"Demam & Godaan Sisa Antibiotik Teman,\" \"Batuk Kering Malam Hari & Kesalahan Sendok Dapur,\" \"Gatal Kulit Alergi & Salep Kortikosteroid Keras Teman,\" and \"Nyeri Lambung (Maag) & Waktu Minum Antasida.\" Each presents choices reflecting real-world medication scenarios and highlights risks like antibiotic resistance, overdosing, inappropriate steroid use, and antacid timing. My focus is on making these interactive and step-by-step.\n\n\n**Structuring Interactive Scenarios**\n\nI\'m structuring the branching scenarios now, focusing on a clear flow: introduction, decision point, pharmaceutical explanation, and a \"When to Ask the Pharmacist\" callout. Each choice leads to a detailed explanation, and I\'m adding options to retry or move on, culminating in a completion badge. I am also working on this modular design to ensure a structured progression for the user.\n\n\n\n**Designing Assessment Modules**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final assessment module, the \"Uji Pemahaman.\" It includes pre- and post-test modes for evaluating literacy gains, with 10 multiple-choice questions curated from core competencies. I\'m building options, including \"Sudah Paham\" for understood concepts, \"Pelajari Lagi\" for revisiting, and category filters. I am also planning a progress tracker.\n\n\n**Refining Assessment Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed rationales, along with citation references, for each answer within the assessment module. I\'m building features for exporting and copying score summaries to aid research data collection, and have added a placeholder for a researcher\'s Google Form questionnaire. Also, I\'m integrating options for immediate feedback or an exam mode with results at the end with a full explanation of each question. Finally, I\'m building a \'tab switcher\' within `LatihanView.tsx` to provide intuitive sub-navigation between \"Skenario Swamedikasi\" and \"Flashcard\" modules. I am focusing on making the entire module user friendly.\n\n\n"
