  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Wiring**\n\nI\'ve been examining `src/App.tsx` and focusing on how `LatihanPreviewView` is connected. I confirmed the import statement at line 19 and quickly identified its usage within the conditional rendering block on line 115, triggered by `currentTab` set to \'latihan\'. The component is rendered only when that condition is true.\n\n\n**Developing Latihan Module**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the actual implementation. My plan is to create `src/views/LatihanView.tsx`, the full view, complete with interactive module implementations, starting with data models: `ScenarioItem`, `FlashcardItem`, and `QuizQuestion`, to be defined in `src/types/latihan.ts` or `src/types/index.ts`. I intend to update `App.tsx` and `BerandaView.tsx` so the interactive sections work. The data structure for these models are defined.\n\n\n**Defining Latihan Data**\n\nI\'m now populating `src/data/latihanData.ts` with detailed scenarios and flashcards. I\'ve drafted four scenarios focused on common clinical pharmacy dilemmas, each addressing patient safety and medication use. I\'m also including twelve flashcards covering key drug classifications and safe medication practices. I am working on the appropriate data structure.\n\n\n**Constructing Quiz Questions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the quiz module. I\'ve designed ten structured quiz questions for both pretest and posttest assessments. Each question will include scores, reviews, explanations, and links to relevant research metrics. I\'m exploring the best way to incorporate skripsi evaluation metrics within the quiz format.\n\n\n**Implementing Quiz Module**\n\nI am now delving into the intricacies of `KuisModule.tsx`. I am focusing on incorporating pretest and posttest modes with a ten-question step-by-step format, complete with progress tracking. I\'m building selection options with immediate feedback and a comprehensive results screen. The results screen will show the final score, assessment level, pretest/posttest comparison, question-by-question reviews, and a \"Copy Results\" feature for easy integration into research questionnaires. I will add tracking with local storage or state with a progress bar and reset option.\n\n\n**Finalizing Prototype Status**\n\nI\'ve just added a new badge indicating \"Phase 2 Active\" for the Latihan & Integrated Evaluation module. I\'ve also implemented deep linking, so users can jump directly to scenario, flashcard, or quiz sections from the Beranda view. The documentation notes have been updated for Skripsi researchers, along with specific requirements. Finally, I\'ve updated the `DOKUMEN_PROTOTIPE_SKRIPSI.md` to reflect the completion of Phase 2, which includes Beranda, Label Checking, Drug Cabinet, Dictionary, Interactive Flashcards, and Quiz evaluation. I also reviewed how to style the 3D flip card, making sure to consider the use of Tailwind CSS.\n\n\n"
