    thinking: "**Inspecting Key Files**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/data/kamusData.ts`, specifically lines 60-131. Previously, I reviewed `latihanData.ts` and `package.json`, and will examine further relevant data files. I need to understand the data structures and how these files contribute to the project\'s overall architecture. I\'m focusing on the `kamusData.ts` section to identify relevant elements.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now investigating the `@google/genai` version in `package.json` \342\200\223 specifically line 14. It seems the current version, `^2.4.0`, may not be sufficient based on the Gemini API skill requirements (lines 263-268), where a version `>= 2.29.1` (or `>= 3.3.0` for `ThinkingLevel.XHIGH`) is preferred. I\'m also considering server-side or client-side `.zip` file parsing. I\'m taking the user\'s prompt seriously as I think about the chatbot\'s architecture.\n\n\n**Evaluating Server Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the Gemini API server-side, given that the application is currently a pure Vite SPA. I am checking `package.json` for details regarding server-side code implementation. Specifically, I am thinking about the Express server setup and how to best call the Gemini API from the server to meet user specifications. I am also checking environment constraints and the preferred method for running server-side code in production.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Scope**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the core features for the chatbot. I envision supporting two methods for adding book sources: direct `.zip` file uploads within the user interface, via a \"Sumber Buku (.zip)\" button, and automatic scanning of a `knowledge_books/` directory on the server, which can be populated with `.zip`, `.txt`, `.md`, or `.pdf` files. This is my focus right now.\n\n\n**Verifying File Extraction**\n\nI am now focusing on robust file extraction. I\'m verifying the best packages for handling `.zip` and `.pdf` files in Node.js, specifically checking `adm-zip`, `jszip`, `pdf-parse`, `unpdf`, and `pdfjs-dist` for compatibility with TypeScript and ESM without DOM or canvas errors. I\'ll need to extract text from `.zip` archives (including various file types like `.txt`, `.md`, `.json`, `.csv`, and `.pdf`), index them, and store the uploaded books in the server\'s `knowledge_books/` directory. I\'m also considering Gemini\'s native PDF support.\n\n\n"
