  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Project Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently looking closely at the project dependencies, specifically `@google/genai` (version 3.3.0), `jszip` (version 3.10.2), and `unpdf` (version 2.1.0). I also intend to quickly verify node compatibility with the existing server code. I will test running the server file with Node v22.23.2 using ESM and TypeScript, using standard erasable TypeScript syntax.\n\n\n**Verifying Node Compatibility**\n\nI\'m now diving into how Node v22.23.2 handles TypeScript imports. Specifically, I\'m verifying the behavior of importing a file (`./foo.ts`) to ensure it\'s seamless with both `.tsx` files and `node server.ts`, given the `tsconfig.json` settings with `\"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true` and `\"noEmit\": true`. This aims for a clean architecture with explicit `.ts` extensions, and no relative imports that could cause problems.\n\n\n**Constructing Knowledge Indexer**\n\nI\'m now focusing on building `/server/knowledgeBase.ts`. This involves creating a website knowledge indexer that reads structured content directly from the website. I will be parsing data from `src/data/*.ts` files, as well as `DOKUMEN_PROTOTIPE_SKRIPSI.md`, and other specific files like `labelHotspots.ts` and `kamusData.ts`. This ensures the chatbot stays updated with the most current website content.\n\n\n**Developing Content Retrieval**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to retrieve the most relevant chunks of text. I\'m building a BM25-inspired retrieval system to process Indonesian and English texts. The system will remove stopwords, score chunks by term frequency, and provide bonuses for exact phrase matches and title matches. I\'m also ensuring balanced retrieval from both website content and book chunks. The text will be split into chunks of approximately 1,200 characters with an overlap of around 180 characters, and labeled by source.\n\n\n**Defining Helper Functions**\n\nI\'ve crafted several helper functions. I have `getKnowledgeSummary()` to list loaded books and website modules. Then, there\'s `ingestUploadedFile()` to upload and index files, and `deleteUploadedBook()` for removing them. I also made a `reloadKnowledgeBase()` function to rescan the directory.\n\n\n\n**Defining Chat API Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/chat` route. I will be handling incoming chat requests with different modes. I\'ll use `gemini-4-hydrogen` for detailed answers in the standard and comprehensive modes and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for the faster mode. The system instructions are tailored for \"Asisten Ruang Obat,\" ensuring clear Indonesian educational responses, adhering to strict ethical guidelines, such as not providing medical advice.\n\n\n**Implementing Source Attribution**\n\nI am now focusing on accurately attributing sources. I will ensure that all responses cite the specific website sections and book sources, using `[Sumber: ...]`. If information is not available in the indexed content, I will clearly state this and offer safe, general guidance, while recommending consultation with a pharmacist or doctor. I will also incorporate reminders for users to seek professional help when red-flag symptoms are mentioned. I\'m also planning to enhance the chat implementation to pass the complete conversation history and the retrieved context chunks, as well as use SSE streaming to provide a responsive, ChatGPT-like user experience. I am checking to make sure that the system returns the used chunks.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating source citation badges like `Website: Cek Label Obat` directly beneath the bot responses. I\'m also ensuring robust error handling for the Gemini API, providing clear messages to the client for issues such as permission errors, invalid API keys, resource exhaustion, or not found errors.\n\nI\'m also setting up the server entrypoint in `/server.ts` to serve several API routes: `/api/health`, `/api/chat`, `/api/knowledge`, `/api/knowledge/upload`, `/api/knowledge/reload`, and `/api/knowledge/:fileName` (DELETE). I\'m configuring Vite middleware in development on port 3000 and static file serving in production. I\'ve updated `package.json` with `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"` to use the newer tool.\n\n\n**Designing Chatbot Drawer**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the chatbot drawer component. I\'m making it accessible app-wide via a floating action button and potentially a quick button in BerandaView or Header. I\'m building a multi-turn scrollable chat with persistent history using `sessionStorage` or `localStorage`. I\'ll also add a \"Percakapan Baru\" button to reset the chat. I\'ll make the chatbot context-aware, offering tailored starter questions based on the current user tab.\n\n\n\n**Defining Knowledge Directory**\n\nI\'m now setting up the directory. I\'m adding a `knowledge_books/README.txt` file and starting on `/server/knowledgeBase.ts`. I also made buttons for uploading and deleting book archives. I\'m implementing compact source tags for AI answers and the disclaimer \"Jawaban berbasis isi Ruang Obat & buku referensi. Bukan diagnosis atau saran dosis pribadi.\" I\'ve included a speed/depth selector.\n\n\n"
