    thinking: "**Analyzing Knowledge Base Code**\n\nI\'m impressed by the clean architecture of `/server/knowledgeBase.ts`. The complete absence of TypeScript parameter properties and enums is noteworthy. Explicit imports, coupled with the support for `.zip` archives containing diverse formats from both the `knowledge_books/` folder and UI uploads, has led me to believe the code is well-structured and highly versatile.\n\n\n**Constructing the Server Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on building `/server.ts`. It leverages Express on port 3000 and mounts `@google/genai` as specified in the `gemini-api` SKILL.md. I\'ve implemented multi-turn chat support with history and system instructions, utilizing `gemini-4-hydrogen` by default, but also incorporating `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for the \"Mode Cepat\" option. I\'m streaming replies via SSE, ensuring a smooth user experience with cited sources in the final event. I\'m also adding comprehensive Gemini error handling to give the user good feedback.\n\n\n"
