    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Structure**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting `TentangModal.tsx`\'s existing structure and comparing it to the earlier prompt requirements for Part 3. I\'ve pinpointed two key sections: \"Tujuan Media Edukasi\" and \"Tim Pengembang Website,\" detailing their current composition. This comparison is driving my next steps in the refactoring process.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the data structures related to the \"Tentang\" section and how it was implemented previously. I recall the user\'s direction to preserve its structure but modify the underlying data. I\'m cross-referencing this with the current `TentangModal.tsx` and the pre-Part 3 setup, paying close attention to the section\'s placement and accessibility before the recent changes. Specifically, I\'m examining how the \"Tujuan Media Edukasi\" and \"Identitas Penelitian / Penyusun\" were handled prior to Part 3, to inform the best way to integrate the new data. I\'m checking which file handled what.\n\n\n**Clarifying Intent and Structure**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the user\'s intent. I\'m recalling Part 3 and verifying what was kept in `TentangModal.tsx`, particularly focusing on whether the user saw that the previous \"Identitas\" section was replaced. I\'m checking if the user thought the \"Tentang\" button in the header was removed. I\'m also confirming what\'s in the footer and homepage, to ensure all sections of `TentangModal.tsx` are easily accessible.\n\n\n**Reviewing Requirements & Context**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in re-reading the prompt, specifically focusing on the instructions to preserve the \"Tentang\" section while updating its data. The user explicitly stated to *not* remove it. I\'m cross-referencing this with the `appConfig.ts` modifications and the previous \"BerandaView.tsx\" structure. I\'m also looking at the attached images for visual reference regarding the desired aesthetics and font choices for the Tentang section.\n\n\n**Visualizing Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now deeply considering the design cues from the images. I\'m noting the editorial serif headings (like Fraunces) and clean sans-serif bodies (like DM Sans), and I\'m visualizing how these will apply to the \"Tentang\" section. I\'m also planning to integrate the warm cream canvas and botanical accents to create the correct mood. I\'m focusing on layout elements like spacing and typographic hierarchy.\n\n\n**Visualizing Color Palette**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color scheme from Image 4, particularly the fourth column, and how this translates to \"Tentang.\" I\'m planning to implement a deep forest green, warm cream, and soft sage green, with terracotta/sand accents. I am considering how the \"MOUNTAIN MEADOW\" aesthetic can inform the section\'s design and user experience. I\'ll need to examine the existing `TentangModal.tsx` file for missing content.\n\n\n**Revisiting Previous Context**\n\nI\'m now re-examining `TentangModal.tsx` more closely, specifically lines 35-119, to compare them against my understanding of the user\'s instructions. I\'m focusing on the \"Identitas Penelitian & Pengembang\" section to understand the discrepancy. I\'m checking if I removed the **Identitas Akademik** card in the preview. I\'m trying to see if the user noticed that the bottom card was hidden.\n\n\n**Confirming Structure & Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now confirming the accessibility and integrity of the \"Tentang\" section. I\'ve verified that the `\"Tentang\"` button in `FooterDisclaimer.tsx` and `\"Tentang Ruang Obat\"` in `BerandaView.tsx` both successfully open `TentangModal`. Inside `TentangModal.tsx`, I\'ll preserve all sections. I need to make sure existing data is in its current structure.\n\n\n**Restoring Typography & Style**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the font restoration. The user prefers Fraunces and DM Sans; this requires reverting Part 3\'s font change to Plus Jakarta Sans. I\'m focusing on `index.html`, `index.css`, `BerandaView.tsx`, and `Header.tsx` to ensure Fraunces, DM Sans, and DM Mono are correctly implemented for headings, body text, and numbers/NIM, respectively, to capture the desired aesthetic. I am confident that restoring these fonts will get us to the Mountain Meadow look.\n\n\n**Envisioning Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now conceptualizing a captivating hero section for `BerandaView.tsx`, inspired by the reference images. I want an editorial, botanical apothecary canvas that evokes a warm, serene feel. The current plain text and small image will evolve into a layered, atmospheric design using warm cream gradients and our existing illustration. I\'ll focus on making this inviting and evocative to users.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Section**\n\nI am now designing the hero section for `BerandaView.tsx`, drawing inspiration from the user\'s references. My focus is crafting an inviting, apothecary-inspired canvas with warm gradients and the existing illustration. I\'m prioritizing editorial typography (Fraunces and DM Sans) and calm aesthetics (green, cream, sand) to evoke a sense of trust with the user.\n\n\n**Refining Sectional Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the content within the existing sections, particularly for the quick summary strip/KPI overview inspired by the images. I aim to create cards that echo the warm, organic feel of Image 1\'s metric cards. I\'m ensuring the \"Skenario Swamedikasi\" quote card maintains its Mountain Meadow serenity. Finally, I\'m checking accessibility and fidelity with all existing sections in `TentangModal.tsx`.\n\n\n**Preserving Project Integrity**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on preserving key project elements. I am confirming I\'m not touching chatbot logic, server files, knowledge base, Gemini models, or API keys, as explicitly stated. I\'m keeping rujukan strings, `identitasProyek.ts` as the single source of truth, and footer without NIMs, while ensuring that the `SHOW_REVIEWER_TOOLS` remains set to false.\n\n\n\n"
