    thinking: "**Revising Modal Component**\n\nI\'m revisiting `TentangModal.tsx` in light of the user\'s latest feedback. I\'m carefully comparing the current implementation against Part 3\'s requirements and the user\'s specific comments, ensuring alignment across all lines of code. The aim is to achieve perfect harmony with the user\'s expectations.\n\n\n**Refining Content Presentation**\n\nI\'m focusing on refining the content presentation, specifically in `TentangModal.tsx`. I need to ensure that the data update retains the aesthetic appeal that I\'m trying to achieve. I\'m carefully evaluating the current content and cross referencing with the user-provided website\'s visual cues for inspiration. I\'m ensuring I\'m not overhauling the existing structure, but maintaining a harmonious balance.\n\n\n**Consolidating Data Display**\n\nI\'m now consolidating the data display within `TentangModal.tsx`. I need to ensure that no information is lost or altered, especially concerning the metadata rows such as \"Tahun\" and \"Penyusun.\" I\'m carefully merging the existing blocks, including **Identitas Akademik & Peneliti**, **Tim Pengembang Website**, **Tujuan Media Edukasi**, **Batasan Produk**, and **Kebijakan Privasi**, making sure the **Tentang Ruang Obat** button remains readily accessible in both `BerandaView` and `FooterDisclaimer`. I also need to focus on designing the visual upgrade to the **opening experience** with the relevant files.\n\n\n**Enhancing Visual Identity**\n\nI\'m now diving into the visual identity, drawing inspiration from the reference screenshots to enhance the *Ruang Obat* domain\'s authenticity. I\'m focusing on restoring the Google Fonts: Fraunces, DM Sans, and DM Mono, to bring a calm, inviting, editorial feel to the site. I\'m also updating the `ModalShell.tsx` title with `font-display font-semibold text-forest`, and working to incorporate the color tokens to align with the cream, botanical sage, and *Mountain Meadow* tones for a polished opening experience.\n\n\n**Crafting a Calm Canvas**\n\nI\'m now implementing the serene, warm editorial hero canvas in `BerandaView.tsx`, drawing inspiration from the visual cues. I\'m focusing on incorporating the gentle gradients and delicate hairline borders, avoiding any overly bright colors or cluttered elements. I\'m also adding a clean editorial kicker, and the interactive `Panduan Fitur` button.\n\n\n**Structuring Hero Components**\n\nI\'m now structuring the hero components within `BerandaView.tsx`, starting with the main split into left and right sections using a grid. On the left side, I\'m integrating an editorial headline and a warm subtitle, both inspired by the visual cues I\'m receiving. I\'m also including primary and secondary CTAs for user engagement. Lastly, I\'m implementing a 3-column trust and pillar row at the bottom, inspired by Image 3. I\'m focusing on text styling such as fonts from Google Fonts: Fraunces, DM Sans, and DM Mono.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Overview Tiles**\n\nI\'m now integrating the 4-tile quick overview strip right below the hero in `BerandaView.tsx`, inspired by Images 1 and 4. This includes tiles for stock recorded, principles of DAGUSIBU, and references from BPOM and Kemenkes. I\'m focusing on making them interactive and providing users with an immediate, calm visual pulse of their medicine cabinet. I\'m also ensuring the visual design is warm and inviting.\n\n\n\n**Designing Tile Interactions**\n\nI\'m now designing the interactive tiles for the quick overview strip. I\'m focusing on making each tile a clickable button with clear actions: \"Di lemari rumah\" clicks to `lemari`, \"Status Aman\" clicks to `lemari` based on `amanCount`, \"Perlu Dicek\" clicks to `lemari` based on `warningCount` or `\'segera\'`, and \"Simulasi Sediaan\" clicks to `cek-label`. I\'m using clean typography, high-contrast colors, and ensuring keyboard accessibility and responsiveness. I\'m aiming for a harmonious visual rhythm and a positive user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Section Transitions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the clean editorial section lead-ins, enhancing visual pacing with `\342\200\224 EKSPLORASI UTAMA`, `\342\200\224 PANTAUAN & LATIHAN`, and `\342\200\224 LITERASI HARIAN`, using `Fraunces` for the headings. I\'m also implementing the dark card for **Skenario Swamedikasi** with a warm *Mountain Meadow* depth and subtle accents. Plus, I\'m ensuring `RingkasanStokObatChart` is clean, crisp and uses `Fraunces` for its heading, and `Belajar Cepat & Edukasi Rumah Tangga` remains warm.\n\n\n"
