    end_line: 578
    content: "---\nname: gemini-interactions-api\ndescription: >\n  Provides coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Covers\n  Interactions API (Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, Omni Flash video,\n  Genie 4 real-time interactive worlds via Live Interactions), Decisions API\n  (gemini-decision-1 for calibrated yes/no, choice, and rubric scoring),\n  general model capabilities (text, image, speech), Lyria music, and Live API.\n  Omni models, Genie 4, and Agents require ai.interactions; gemini-decision-1\n  requires ai.decisions.create. Use for Interactions API, Decisions API,\n  Antigravity, Deep Research, Omni video, Genie 4 interactive worlds, or\n  calibrated classification/rubric scoring.\n---\n\n# Gemini Interactions API\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n-   **JavaScript/TypeScript**: `@google/genai` >= `2.4.0` \342\206\222 `npm install\n    @google/genai`\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> The Interactions API requires `@google/genai` version `2.4.0` or later. If\n> your `package.json` has a `1.x.x` version, you must explicitly upgrade by\n> running `npm i @google/genai@latest` or `npm i @google/genai@^2.4.0`. A simple\n> `npm update` will not cross the major version boundary.\n\n## @google/genai Models\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> The models listed in this section are the absolute source of truth when\n> selecting a model. Even if a specific use case is not listed in the examples\n> or sections below, you must still choose one of the models defined here,\n> unless the user specifies one.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **NEVER** use the following deprecated models. They are strictly prohibited\n> and unsupported: - `gemini-1.5-flash` - `gemini-1.5-pro` - `gemini-pro`\n>\n> Always select a valid model from the list below.\n\n-   If the user provides a full model name that includes hyphens, a version, and\n    an optional date (e.g., gemini-2.5-flash-preview-12-2025 or\n    gemini-3.1-pro-preview), use it directly.\n-   If the user provides a common name or alias, use the following full model\n    name.\n    -   gemini flash, gemini 4 flash, gemini hydrogen, or gemini 4 hydrogen:\n        \'gemini-4-hydrogen\'\n    -   gemini lite or flash lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'\n    -   gemini carbon or gemini 4 carbon: \'gemini-4-carbon\'\n    -   gemini pro, gemini 4, gemini neon, or gemini 4 neon: \'gemini-4-neon\'\n    -   gemini argon or gemini 4 argon: \'gemini-4-argon\'\n    -   nano banana, or gemini flash image, or nano banana lite, or nano banana\n        2 lite: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   nano banana 2.1: \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   nano banana pro, or gemini pro image: \'gemini-3-pro-image\'\n    -   native audio, gemini live, or gemini flash audio: \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   gemini live extended thinking or thinker talker:\n        \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   gemini transcribe or audio transcription: \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   live transcribe or live translation: \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   gemini tts, gemini text-to-speech, or gemini flash lite tts:\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   gemini flash tts: \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   gemini omni flash, Veo, or Veo lite: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\'\n    -   genie, genie 4, or interactive world model: \'genie-4\'\n    -   Lyria Clip: \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Lyria Pro: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n    -   gemini embedding or gemini embedding 2: \'gemini-embedding-2\'\n    -   gemini decision, gemini decision 1, or decisions api:\n        \'gemini-decision-1\'\n-   If the user does not specify any model, select the following model based on\n    the task type.\n    -   Basic Text Tasks (e.g., summarization, proofreading, and simple Q&A):\n        \'gemini-4-hydrogen\'\n    -   Complex Text Tasks (e.g., advanced reasoning, coding, math, and STEM):\n        \'gemini-4-neon\'\n    -   Deep Reasoning Tasks pushing reasoning depth (e.g., complex root-cause\n        debugging, architectural design, scientific proofs, and security\n        auditing): \'gemini-4-carbon\'\n    -   General Image Generation and Editing Tasks:\n        \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\'\n    -   High-Quality Image Generation and Editing Tasks (supports 1K, 2K, and 4K\n        resolution): \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\'\n    -   Audio Transcription Tasks (pre-recorded or static audio via Interactions\n        or generateContent): \'gemini-3.5-transcribe\'\n    -   Video Generation, Editing, and Extension Tasks: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\'\n    -   Real-time Interactive World Generation & Simulation Tasks (720p @ 24 fps\n        video + 48 kHz stereo audio via Live Interactions API): \'genie-4\'\n    -   Real-time audio & video conversation tasks (via Live API):\n        \'gemini-3.8-live\'\n    -   Real-time voice conversation tasks requiring complex reasoning or\n        multi-step tool use (via Live API): \'gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\'\n    -   Real-time speech translation and live audio transcription tasks (via\n        Live API): \'gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\'\n    -   General Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g., article reading, global\n        dubbing/localization, customer service IVR, accessibility screen\n        readers, and high-throughput voice assistants):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\'\n    -   Voice Design, Screenplay, and Podcasting Text-to-Speech Tasks (e.g.,\n        prompting custom voice personas from scratch, dual-speaker screenplay\n        editing, and dialogue apps requiring backchanneling like `|mhm|` or\n        `|yeah|` and vocal bursts like `<laugh>` or `<gasp>`):\n        \'gemini-3.8-flash-tts\'\n    -   Short music clip generation tasks (30s): \'lyria-3-clip-preview\'\n    -   Full-length music generation tasks: \'lyria-3-pro-preview\'\n    -   Embedding tasks: \'gemini-embedding-2\'\n    -   Calibrated yes/no checks, multi-class routing/classification, policy\n        checks, or rubric scoring tasks (via Decisions API): \'gemini-decision-1\'\n\nThe following models require a paid API key. Prompt the user to select one by\ncalling the `show_aistudio_ui` tool with arguments: `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"`\n*before* using these models.\n\n-   `gemini-4-carbon`\n-   `gemini-4-neon`\n-   `gemini-4-argon`\n-   `gemini-3-pro-image`\n-   `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`\n-   `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`\n-   `gemini-omni-1.2-flash`\n-   `genie-4`\n-   `lyria-3-clip-preview`\n-   `lyria-3-pro-preview`\n\n## @google/genai Agents\n\nThe following agents are available for use with the Interactions API:\n\n-   `antigravity-preview-09-2026`: Antigravity Agent \342\200\224 general-purpose managed\n    agent with code execution, file management, and web access in a sandboxed\n    Linux environment.\n-   `deep-research-preview-04-2026`: Deep Research \342\200\224 fast, interactive\n-   `deep-research-max-preview-04-2026`: Deep Research Max \342\200\224 maximum\n    exhaustiveness\n-   **Custom agents**: Create your own via `ai.agents.create()`.\n\nAll agents require a paid API key. Prompt the user to select one by calling the\n`show_aistudio_ui` tool with arguments: `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"` *before*\nusing any agent.\n\n## Important Additional Notes\n\n-   Interactions are **stored by default** (`store=true`). Paid tier retains for\n    55 days, free tier for 1 day.\n-   Set `store=false` to opt out, but this disables `previous_interaction_id`\n    and `background=true`.\n-   `tools`, `system_instruction`, and `generation_config` are\n    **interaction-scoped**, re-specify them each turn.\n-   **Managed agents** require `environment=\"remote\"` (or an environment ID /\n    config object) to provision a sandbox.\n-   **Migrating from `generateContent`**: Always confirm scope with the user\n    before editing.\n\n## Agent-Specific Guidance\n\n> **Note:** `ai.environments`, `ai.environments.files`, and `ai.credentials`\n> require `@google/genai >= 2.25.0` (`npm i @google/genai@latest`).\n\nCall `view_file` on the matching `references/*.md` file in this skill\'s\ndirectory (relative to this `SKILL.md` path) before implementing an agent:\n\nAgent / Capability          | Reference File                                                                                                     | When to Read\n:-------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-----------\n**Managed Agents Overview** | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/managed-agents.md`](references/managed-agents.md)       | Polling, multi-turn state (`previous_interaction_id` + `environment`), streaming, and downloading sandbox files.\n**Antigravity Agent**       | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/antigravity-agent.md`](references/antigravity-agent.md) | Default agent (`antigravity-preview-09-2026`), `agent_config` model selection & token budget, tools, and multimodal input.\n**Custom Agents**           | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/custom-agents.md`](references/custom-agents.md)         | Creating custom agents (`ai.agents.create`), inline/repo sources, network rules, and custom instructions.\n**Deep Research Agent**     | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/deep-research.md`](references/deep-research.md)         | `deep-research-preview-04-2026` / `deep-research-max-preview-04-2026`, collaborative planning, visualization, streaming, MCP, and file search.\n**Agent Environments**      | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/agent-environment.md`](references/agent-environment.md) | Sandbox configuration (`ai.environments`), custom sources, network allowlist, and environment files (`ai.environments.files`).\n**Agent Credentials**       | [`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/agent-credentials.md`](references/agent-credentials.md) | Server-managed secrets (`ai.credentials`), bearer tokens, OAuth2, environment variables, network allowlist & MCP credential injection.\n\n## Modality & Tool Reference Files\n\nCall `view_file` on the matching `references/*.md` file in this skill\'s\ndirectory (relative to this `SKILL.md` path) before implementing:\n\n-   **Tools, Grounding, JSON, Streaming & Embeddings**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/tools_and_grounding.md`](references/tools_and_grounding.md)):\n    `response_format` JSON Schema, `stream: true` SSE streaming, custom\n    `function_call` / `function_result`, Google Search (`google_search`), URL\n    context (`url_context`), Google Maps (`google_maps`), and\n    `ai.models.embedContent` (`gemini-embedding-2`).\n-   **Image, Music & Video Generation**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/image_video_music.md`](references/image_video_music.md)):\n    Image generation/editing (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`,\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`, `gemini-3-pro-image`), music generation with\n    `lyria-3-clip-preview` / `lyria-3-pro-preview`, and video generation,\n    editing, and extension with `gemini-omni-1.2-flash`\n    (`response_format: { type: \'video\', ... }`).\n-   **Interactive World Generation (Genie 4)**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/genie-4-live-world.md`](references/genie-4-live-world.md)):\n    Real-time interactive 720p @ 24 fps video + 48 kHz stereo audio worlds with\n    `genie-4` (`models/genie-4`) over Live Interactions (`v1beta`, server-minted\n    ephemeral `authTokens.create` + browser WebRTC `ai.interactions.connect`,\n    `world_setup`, `user_action`, mid-session `input`, and\n    `session.complete()`).\n-   **Audio Transcription & TTS**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/speech_and_audio.md`](references/speech_and_audio.md)):\n    Pre-recorded audio input transcription (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`) and\n    single-speaker / multi-speaker text-to-speech (`gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts`,\n    `gemini-3.8-flash-tts`, `speech_config`, `speech_config.speakers`,\n    `speech_metadata` annotations, inline audio tags).\n-   **Live API**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/live_api.md`](references/live_api.md)):\n    Real-time bidirectional voice/video streaming via `ai.live.connect`\n    (`gemini-3.8-live`, `gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking`), live transcription\n    and speech translation (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`, `translationConfig`),\n    PCM audio encoding/decoding, interruption handling, and Live API rules.\n-   **Decisions API**\n    ([`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/decisions-api.md`](references/decisions-api.md)):\n    Calibrated yes/no (`noul`), single-select (`choice`), and rubric (`score`)\n    evaluations over shared multimodal input with zero output tokens\n    (`ai.decisions.create`, `gemini-decision-1`).\n\n## @google/genai Coding Guidelines\n\nUse the `@google/genai` SDK to call Gemini agents.\n\n### Calling Gemini Interactions API\n\n-   **Always** call Gemini Interactions API from the server-side code of the\n    application (except the browser WebRTC media client for `genie-4`, which\n    connects with a server-minted ephemeral token per\n    `references/genie-4-live-world.md`).\n-   **NEVER** call Gemini Interactions API directly from the client/browser code\n    using `GEMINI_API_KEY` (only `genie-4` WebRTC `interactions.connect` runs in\n    the browser, authenticated exclusively with an ephemeral token minted on the\n    server via `interactions.authTokens.create`).\n-   **NEVER** expose the API key to the browser.\n-   **No Static Explanatory UI or Chat Explanations**: Do **not** explain how\n    agents (like Antigravity or Deep Research) work in your chat responses, and\n    do **not** generate static informational UI components (such as \"About\"\n    cards or help paragraphs) explaining the sandbox container infrastructure in\n    the code, unless explicitly requested. However, you **should** build dynamic\n    UI elements (often referred to as showing \"proof of work\") to display the\n    agent\'s live progress, sub-steps, reasoning thoughts, and tool calls from\n    the `interaction.steps` response.\n-   **Agents and Omni models require Interactions API**: Managed agents (such as\n    `antigravity-preview-09-2026` or `deep-research-preview-04-2026`), custom\n    agents, and Omni models (like `gemini-omni-1.2-flash`) can **ONLY** be\n    invoked using the `ai.interactions.create()` method. They **cannot** be\n    invoked using `ai.models.generateContent()` or\n    `ai.models.generateContentStream()`. Calling a model using `generateContent`\n    is only for standard models (like `gemini-4-hydrogen`), not agents or Omni\n    models.\n-   **`gemini-decision-1` requires Decisions API**: Read\n    `references/decisions-api.md` via `view_file` first (do not inspect\n    `node_modules`), and invoke bare `model: \"gemini-decision-1\"` **ONLY** via\n    `ai.decisions.create()` (never `interactions.create` or `generateContent`).\n-   **Strict Lowercase `response_modalities`**: When calling\n    `ai.interactions.create`, the `response_modalities` parameter strictly\n    requires lowercase string literals: `\'text\'`, `\'image\'`, `\'audio\'`,\n    `\'video\'`, `\'document\'`. **NEVER** pass uppercase strings (e.g. `[\'AUDIO\']`,\n    `[\'TEXT\']`) or `Modality` enum values (e.g. `[Modality.AUDIO]`). The backend\n    Interactions API strictly validates this field and will fail with `400 The\n    value \'AUDIO\' is not supported for \'response_modalities[0]\'. Supported\n    values: \'text\', \'image\', \'audio\', \'video\', \'document\'`.\n\nThe server handles all `@google/genai` SDK calls. The client communicates with\nthe server through your application\'s API endpoints (e.g., Next.js API routes,\nExpress routes, or Angular SSR endpoints).\n\nIf a server-side Interactions or Decisions API call fails or errors, propagate\nthe error back to the client (via the HTTP response, SSE stream, or WebSocket)\nso the frontend can display it\342\200\224never return simulated or heuristic fallbacks.\n\n### Server-Side Initialization\n\nCreate a shared Gemini client utility on the server:\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\nconst ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\n```\n\n### Client-Side Usage\n\nThe client never imports `@google/genai` (except the `genie-4` ephemeral-token\nWebRTC client in `references/genie-4-live-world.md`, which never receives\n`GEMINI_API_KEY`). Instead, it calls your server\'s API routes, for example:\n\n```ts\nconst response = await fetch(\"/api/research\", {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: \"Research the history of Google TPUs.\" }),\n});\nconst { interactionId } = await response.json();\n```\n\n### Incorrect Usages\n\nDo *not* use or import the following types from `@google/genai`; these are\ndeprecated APIs and no longer work.\n\n-   **Incorrect** `GoogleGenerativeAI`\n-   **Incorrect** `google.generativeai`\n-   **Incorrect** `models.create`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models.create`\n-   **Incorrect** `models.getGenerativeModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `genAI.getGenerativeModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models.getModel`\n-   **Incorrect** `ai.models[\'model_name\']`\n-   **Incorrect** `generationConfig`\n-   **Incorrect** `GoogleGenAIError`\n-   **Incorrect** `GenerateContentResult`; **Correct**\n    `GenerateContentResponse`.\n-   **Incorrect** `GenerateContentRequest`; **Correct**\n    `GenerateContentParameters`.\n-   **Incorrect** `SchemaType`; **Correct** `Type`.\n-   **Incorrect** `response_modalities: [\'AUDIO\']` or `response_modalities:\n    [Modality.AUDIO]`; **Correct** `response_modalities: [\'audio\']`\n    (Interactions API `response_modalities` strictly requires lowercase string\n    literals: `\'text\'`, `\'image\'`, `\'audio\'`, `\'video\'`, `\'document\'`).\n-   **Incorrect** `responseModalities: [...]` inside `ai.interactions.create`;\n    **Correct** `response_modalities: [\'audio\']` (`snake_case` in Interactions\n    API vs `camelCase` in `generateContent`).\n\nDo *not* import `@google/genai` or instantiate `GoogleGenAI` in any client-side\n/ browser code unless using the `genie-4` ephemeral-token WebRTC client\n(`references/genie-4-live-world.md`) or when the user explicitly asks for it (in\nwhich case highlight the security implications of exposing an API key). All\nGemini SDK usage must be server-side by default.\n\n### API Key\n\n-   **Server-only:** The API key is accessed via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` on\n    the server. It must **never** be sent to the browser or included in\n    client-side bundles.\n-   **Incorrect Initialization:** `const ai = new GoogleGenAI(apiKey);` // Must\n    use a named parameter `{ apiKey: ... }`.\n-   **No UI for API Key:** Do **not** generate any UI elements (input fields,\n    forms, prompts, configuration sections) or code snippets for entering or\n    managing the API key. Do **not** request that the user update the API key in\n    the code. The key\'s availability is handled externally and is a hard\n    requirement. The application **must not** ask the user for it under any\n    circumstances.\n\n### Import\n\n-   **SDK Version:** Ensure `@google/genai >= 2.32.0` in `package.json`\n    (`>= 3.1.0` for `\"xhigh\"` `ThinkingLevel`; `>= 3.2.0` and client\n    `apiVersion: \"v1beta\"` for `ai.decisions.create` / `gemini-decision-1` \342\200\224\n    keep a separate client if other routes use `3.x` `v1` defaults; `>= 3.5.0`\n    with `apiVersion: \"v1beta\"` only when using `genie-4`\n    `ai.interactions.connect` / `ai.interactions.authTokens`). Only run\n    `npm i @google/genai@latest` when the installed version is below the minimum\n    required for the feature in use (`npm update` does not cross major\n    versions).\n-   Always use `import {GoogleGenAI} from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `import { GoogleGenerativeAI } from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `import type { GoogleGenAI} from \"@google/genai\";`\n-   **Prohibited:** `declare var GoogleGenAI`.\n-   **Prohibited:** Any `@google/genai` import in client-side code, except the\n    `genie-4` ephemeral-token WebRTC client\n    (`references/genie-4-live-world.md`).\n\n## Data Model\n\nAn `Interaction` response contains `steps`, an array of typed step objects\nrepresenting a structured timeline of the interaction turn.\n\n### Step Types\n\n**User steps:**\n\n-   `user_input`: User input (text, audio, multimodal). Contains `content`\n    array.\n\n**Model/server steps:**\n\n-   `model_output`: Final model generation. Contains `content` array with\n    `text`, `image`, `audio`, etc.\n-   `thought`: Model reasoning/Chain of Thought. Has `signature` field\n    (required) and optional `summary` (an array of\n    `{ type: \'text\', text: string }` content parts \342\200\224 extract text via\n    `step.summary?.map(c => c.text).join(\'\')`, never render `step.summary`\n    directly as a string/React child).\n-   `function_call`: Tool call request (`id`, `name`, `arguments`).\n-   `function_result`: Tool result you send back (`call_id`, `name`, `result`).\n-   `google_search_call` / `google_search_result`: Google Search tool steps, can\n    have a `signature` field.\n-   `code_execution_call` / `code_execution_result`: Code execution tool steps,\n    can have a `signature` field. On `@google/genai >= 3.0.0`,\n    `CodeExecutionResultStep.result` is typed as `Array<Content> | string`;\n    narrow with `typeof step.result === \"string\"` before reading it as text.\n-   `url_context_call` / `url_context_result`: URL context tool steps, can have\n    a `signature` field.\n-   `mcp_server_tool_call` / `mcp_server_tool_result`: Remote MCP tool steps.\n-   `file_search_call` / `file_search_result`: File search tool steps, can have\n    a `signature` field.\n\n### Content types (inside `content` array)\n\n-   `text`: Text content (`text` field)\n-   `image` / `audio` / `document` / `video`: Content with `data`, `mime_type`,\n    or `uri`\n\n### Response Helpers\n\nThe SDK provides convenience properties on the `Interaction` response object:\n\n-   `output_text` (`string | null`): The last consecutive run of text from the\n    trailing `model_output` steps.\n-   `output_image` (`Image | null`): The last image generated by the model.\n    Returns an object with `data` (base64) and `mime_type`.\n-   `output_audio` (`Audio | null`): The last audio generated by the model.\n    Returns an object with `data` (base64) and `mime_type`.\n-   `output_video` (`Video | null`): The last video generated by the model.\n    Returns an object with `data` (base64) or `uri`, and `mime_type`.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n>\n> During long-running agent execution (such as Antigravity, custom agents, or\n> Deep Research), the agent generates output incrementally across multiple\n> chronological `model_output` steps (e.g., intermediate drafts, code execution\n> outputs, and sections) as it runs, rather than writing everything in a single\n> step. Because `output_text` only returns the text from the **very last\n> consecutive step**, using `interaction.output_text` on an agent result may cut\n> off the response, showing only the concluding section and losing the earlier\n> sections. For all agent interactions, you should iterate and combine the text\n> parts from all `model_output` steps in the `steps` array:\n>\n> ```typescript\n> let fullOutput = \"\";\n> for (const step of interaction.steps) {\n>   if (step.type === \'model_output\') {\n>     const textContent = step.content?.find(c => c.type === \'text\');\n>     if (textContent && textContent.text) {\n>       fullOutput += textContent.text;\n>     }\n>   }\n> }\n> ```\n\n### Safe JSON Extraction from Agent Output\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> Standard model calls support structured outputs natively (using\n> `response_format`), but **managed agents (like Antigravity and Deep Research)\n> do not support structured outputs**. If you need structured JSON from an\n> agent, you must ask for it in the text prompt (instructing the agent to write\n> JSON). Because this relies on text instructions, the agent may wrap it in\n> markdown code blocks or append conversational text. Use the following regex\n> matching pattern to safely extract and parse the JSON from the combined steps\n> output:\n\n````typescript\nlet parsedReport = null;\nconst jsonMatch =\n  fullOutput.match(/```json\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*```/) ||\n  fullOutput.match(/([\\{\\[][\\s\\S]*[\\}\\]])/);\nif (jsonMatch) {\n  try {\n    parsedReport = JSON.parse(jsonMatch[1]);\n  } catch (err) {\n    // Implement lenient cleanup logic to catch trailing commas or shell\n    // outputs inside the code blocks\n  }\n}\n````\n\n## General Interactions Examples\n\nCreate a simple model interaction with a text input.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  input: \"why is the sky blue?\",\n});\nconsole.log(interaction.output_text);\n```\n\n### System Instruction and Other Model Configs\n\nCreate an interaction with a system instruction and other model configs.\n\nNote: The `max_output_tokens` parameter includes both response tokens and\nthinking (reasoning) tokens. It is recommended to specify the desired response\nsize within `system_instruction` rather than using `max_output_tokens`. Do not\npass deprecated sampling parameters (`temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`) to\n`gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-neon`, `gemini-4-argon`, or `gemini-4-carbon`.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  input: \"Tell me a story.\",\n  system_instruction: \"You are a storyteller for kids under 5 years old.\",\n  generation_config: {\n    seed: 42,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Thinking Config\n\n`thinking_level` in `generation_config` controls reasoning depth on Gemini 4 and\nGemini 3 models (use lowercase strings in `ai.interactions.create`; do **NOT**\nset `thinking_budget` on `gemini-4-neon`, `gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-argon`,\nor `gemini-4-carbon`, which returns a 400 error):\n\n-   `\"xhigh\"`: Maximum reasoning depth on `gemini-4-neon` and\n    `gemini-4-hydrogen` (complex multi-step agentic workflows, open-ended\n    research, multi-document synthesis). **Only** supported on `gemini-4-neon`\n    and `gemini-4-hydrogen` \342\200\224 returns a 400 error on `gemini-4-argon`,\n    `gemini-4-carbon`, and Gemini 3 models.\n-   `\"high\"`: Default for `gemini-4-neon` and `gemini-4-hydrogen`; maximum\n    reasoning depth on `gemini-4-argon`, `gemini-4-carbon`, and Gemini 3 models.\n-   `\"medium\"`: Default for `gemini-4-argon` and `gemini-4-carbon`; faster\n    responses and lower token use on `gemini-4-neon` and `gemini-4-hydrogen`.\n-   `\"low\"`: Lowest latency and token cost (e.g., game AI opponents, fast chat).\n-   `\"minimal\"`: Default for `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` only; **not** supported on\n    `gemini-4-neon`, `gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-argon`, or `gemini-4-carbon`\n    (400 error).\n\nOmit `thinking_level` by default unless the task needs lower latency (`\"low\"` /\n`\"medium\"`) or deeper reasoning (`\"xhigh\"` on `gemini-4-neon` /\n`gemini-4-hydrogen`, or `\"high\"` on `gemini-4-argon` / `gemini-4-carbon`):\n\n```ts\ngeneration_config: { thinking_level: \"low\" } // or \"xhigh\" on gemini-4-neon / gemini-4-hydrogen\n```\n\n### Multi-turn Interactions\n\nUse `previous_interaction_id` to chain interactions for multi-turn\nconversations.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\nconst interaction2 = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \"gemini-4-hydrogen\",\n  input: \"How are you?\",\n  previous_interaction_id: interaction1.id,\n});\n```\n\n### API Error Handling\n\n-   Implement robust handling for API errors (e.g., network issues, 4xx/5xx\n    responses).\n-   Use graceful retry logic (like exponential backoff) to avoid overwhelming\n    the backend and improve reliability.\n-   Return meaningful error responses from API endpoints so the client can\n    display appropriate messages.\n-   If you receive a `PERMISSION_DENIED` (403) or `API_KEY_INVALID` (400) error\n    from the Gemini API, or if the user reports this error in their application,\n    ask the user to check the API key (or select one if not set) in the\n    **Settings > Secrets** panel.\n-   If you receive a `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (429) error while using a free tier\n    api key, it might be because you are accessing a paid-only model. Advise the\n    user that upgrading to a paid tier increases their quota, and that they can\n    use the **Settings > Secrets** panel to select a billing enabled API key.\n-   If you encounter a `NOT_FOUND` (404) error when calling the Gemini API, or\n    if the user reports a 404 error, it typically indicates that the requested\n    model is invalid or unsupported. You **MUST** verify and update the model\n    name to one of the active models defined in the **## @google/genai Models**\n    section.\n-   If you fail to parse the interaction output response (e.g., properties like\n    `steps` or `output_text` are undefined or throw errors), check the SDK\n    version in `package.json`. If the installed `@google/genai` version is\n    `1.x.x` (or less than `2.4.0`), you **MUST** upgrade it to\n    `@google/genai@latest` (or `^2.4.0`) by running `npm i @google/genai@latest`\n    on the server, as legacy versions do not support the new steps schema.\n-   If `ai.decisions` is undefined or `decisions.create` returns `404`, upgrade\n    with `npm i @google/genai@latest` (`>= 3.2.0`), set `apiVersion: \"v1beta\"`\n    on `new GoogleGenAI(...)`, and pass bare `model: \"gemini-decision-1\"`.\n"
    num_lines: 579
    num_bytes: 29091
    is_skill_file: true
    skill_metadata {
      name: "gemini-interactions-api"
      description: "Provides coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Covers Interactions API (Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, Omni Flash video, Genie 4 real-time interactive worlds via Live Interactions), Decisions API (gemini-decision-1 for calibrated yes/no, choice, and rubric scoring), general model capabilities (text, image, speech), Lyria music, and Live API. Omni models, Genie 4, and Agents require ai.interactions; gemini-decision-1 requires ai.decisions.create. Use for Interactions API, Decisions API, Antigravity, Deep Research, Omni video, Genie 4 interactive worlds, or calibrated classification/rubric scoring."
    }
    line_range_bytes: 29091
  }
}
