    end_line: 442
    content: "# Gemini Interactions API \342\200\224 Image, Music (Lyria) & Video (Omni Flash) Generation\n\n### Image Generation and Editing\n\nGenerate images using `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` by default.\n\n#### Examples\n\nUse `ai.interactions.create` to generate images with nano banana series models\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\',\n  input: \"A robot holding a red skateboard.\",\n  response_modalities: [\'image\', \'text\'],\n  generation_config: {\n    image_config: {\n      aspect_ratio: \"1:1\",\n      image_size: \"1K\"\n    },\n  },\n});\nfor (const step of interaction.steps) {\n  if (step.type === \'model_output\') {\n    const imageContent = step.content?.find(c => c.type === \'image\');\n    if (imageContent && imageContent.data) {\n      const base64EncodeString: string = imageContent.data;\n      const mimeType = imageContent.mime_type || \'image/png\';\n      const imageUrl = `data:${mimeType};base64,${base64EncodeString}`;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nTo edit images:\n\n```ts\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\',\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      data: base64ImageData,\n      mime_type: \"image/png\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      text: \"can you add a llama next to the image\",\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n### Music Generation (Lyria)\n\nGenerate music from a text prompt, optionally combined with an image. Two models\nare available:\n\n-   `lyria-3-clip-preview` (**Lyria Clip**): Short clips up to 30 seconds.\n-   `lyria-3-pro-preview` (**Lyria Pro**): Full-length tracks.\n\nBoth models use the same streaming API and return audio in the same format.\n\n-   Use `generateContentStream` with `responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO]`.\n-   The response stream contains both audio (`inlineData`) and text (lyrics and\n    metadata) parts. Accumulate the base64-encoded audio chunks, then decode\n    into a playable Blob.\n-   Unlike Live and streaming TTS (which return raw PCM requiring\n    `AudioContext`), these models return encoded audio (e.g., WAV). Use `atob`\n    and `Blob` for playback.\n-   When using Lyria models, users **MUST** select their own API key. Prompt\n    them to set it in AI Studio Settings > Secrets > GEMINI_API_KEY before using\n    these models.\n\n#### Text-Only Music Generation\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Modality } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  // \"lyria-3-clip-preview\" or \"lyria-3-pro-preview\" (full tracks)\n  model: \"lyria-3-clip-preview\",\n  contents: \'Generate a 30-second cinematic orchestral track.\',\n});\n\nlet audioBase64 = \"\";\nlet lyrics = \"\";\nlet mimeType = \"audio/wav\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of response) {\n  const parts = chunk.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts;\n  if (!parts) continue;\n\n  for (const part of parts) {\n    if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n      if (!audioBase64 && part.inlineData.mimeType) {\n        mimeType = part.inlineData.mimeType;\n      }\n      audioBase64 += part.inlineData.data;\n    }\n    if (part.text && !lyrics) {\n      // The first text part contains the generated lyrics.\n      lyrics = part.text;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Decode base64 audio into a playable Blob URL\nconst binary = atob(audioBase64);\nconst bytes = new Uint8Array(binary.length);\nfor (let i = 0; i < binary.length; i++) {\n  bytes[i] = binary.charCodeAt(i);\n}\nconst blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: mimeType });\nconst audioUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n```\n\n#### Image + Text Music Generation\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Modality } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  // \"lyria-3-clip-preview\" or \"lyria-3-pro-preview\" (full tracks)\n  model: \"lyria-3-clip-preview\",\n  contents: {\n    parts: [\n      { text: \'Generate a 30-second track inspired by this image.\' },\n      { inlineData: { data: base64ImageData, mimeType: \"image/jpeg\" } },\n    ],\n  },\n});\n// Process the stream identically to the text-only example above.\n```\n\n### Video Generation, Editing, and Extension (Omni Flash)\n\nGenerate, edit, and extend videos using the `gemini-omni-1.2-flash` model.\n\nNote: Video generation is a long-running operation. You can run it synchronously\n(with a high timeout) or in the background (`background: true`) and poll for the\nresult. Set `store: true` (the default) if the generated video may be edited or\nextended in subsequent turns via `previous_interaction_id`; setting\n`store: false` disables multi-turn follow-ups on that video.\n\n#### 1. Text-to-Video (Synchronous)\n\nGenerate a video directly from a detailed prompt. Use `response_format` to\nspecify output parameters like aspect ratio, duration, and resolution.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  input:\n    \'A hyper-realistic close-up of an elephant drinking a large cup of tea.\',\n  background: false,\n  store: false, // Set to true if you plan to edit or extend this video later\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: {\n    type: \'video\',\n    aspect_ratio: \'16:9\', // \'16:9\' (default) or \'9:16\'\n    duration: \'10s\',      // \'3s\' to \'15s\' in 1s increments (\'10s\' default; \'3s\' to \'10s\' for 2-frame interpolation)\n    resolution: \'720p\',   // \'360p\', \'720p\' (default), \'1080p\', or \'4k\'\n  }\n}, { timeout: 300000 }); // 5 minutes timeout\n\nconst videoPart = interaction.output_video;\nif (videoPart && videoPart.data) {\n  const videoBuffer = Buffer.from(videoPart.data, \'base64\');\n  // Save videoBuffer to file or send to client\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Image-to-Video (Animate Image)\n\nProvide a starting frame image and a motion prompt.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      mime_type: \"image/png\",\n      data: base64ImageBytes,\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      text:\n        \"Cherry blossom petals gently fall while a breeze ripples through\" +\n        \" the garden pond.\",\n    }\n  ],\n  background: false,\n  store: false,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: {\n    type: \'video\',\n    aspect_ratio: \'16:9\',\n  }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\nconst videoPart = interaction.output_video;\nif (videoPart && videoPart.data) {\n  const videoBuffer = Buffer.from(videoPart.data, \'base64\');\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Storyboard Reference (Multiple Images)\n\nSupply up to 6 reference images (including on `\'15s\'` clips) to guide video\ngeneration. You can pass multiple images in `input` (describing how each\nreference image should be used in natural language, or passing two images as\nstarting and ending frames for keyframe interpolation up to `\'10s\'`) or mix\nstored interactions (via `previous_interaction_id`) and inline data. Short\nreference videos (~3s each; up to 3 for `\'3s\'`\342\200\223`\'10s\'` clips and at most 1 for\n`\'11s\'`\342\200\223`\'15s\'` clips) are also supported when generating a new video, whereas\nreference images work across generation, video editing, and video extension.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\n// Generate first reference image (stored)\nconst r1 = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\',\n  input: \'A cute tabby cat with a blue collar, portrait\',\n  store: true,\n  response_format: { type: \'image\' }\n});\n\n// Generate second reference image (not stored)\nconst r2 = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\',\n  input: \'A colorful ball of yarn on a wooden floor\',\n  store: false,\n  response_format: { type: \'image\' }\n});\nconst yarnImage = r2.output_image;\n\n// Generate video combining both\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  previous_interaction_id: r1.id, // References the cat image\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \'image\',\n      mime_type: yarnImage?.mime_type ?? \'image/png\',\n      data: yarnImage?.data ?? \'\',\n    },\n    {\n      type: \'text\',\n      text:\n        \'The cat is playfully batting at the ball of yarn on a wooden floor.\'\n    }\n  ],\n  background: false,\n  store: true,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: {\n    type: \'video\',\n    aspect_ratio: \'16:9\'\n  }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\nconst videoPart = interaction.output_video;\n// ...\n```\n\n#### 4. Video-to-Video Editing\n\nModify an existing video by providing the video and an editing instruction (you\ncan also include reference image(s) alongside the video in `input` or with\n`previous_interaction_id` to swap in a character, object, or visual style; only\nreference videos are restricted to new video generation). For uploaded videos,\nupload via the Files API (`ai.files.upload`) and poll `ai.files.get` until\n`state === \'ACTIVE\'` before passing `videoFile.uri` (small videos can also be\npassed inline via `data` and `mime_type: \'video/mp4\'`).\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\n// 1. Upload video using the Files API and wait until processing completes\nlet videoFile = await ai.files.upload({\n  file: \'input_video.mp4\',\n  config: { mimeType: \'video/mp4\' },\n});\n\nwhile (videoFile.state === \'PROCESSING\') {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 10000));\n  videoFile = await ai.files.get({ name: videoFile.name || \'\' });\n}\nif (videoFile.state === \'FAILED\') {\n  throw new Error(\'Video processing failed.\');\n}\n\n// 2. Edit the uploaded video\nconst interaction = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \'video\',\n      uri: videoFile.uri,\n    },\n    {\n      type: \'text\',\n      text:\n        \'Change the dog to a tabby cat. Keep everything else the same.\',\n    }\n  ],\n  background: false,\n  store: false,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: {\n    type: \'video\',\n  }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\nconst videoPart = interaction.output_video;\n// ...\n```\n\n#### 5. Multi-turn Video Editing (Chat)\n\nTo perform iterative edits, pass the `previous_interaction_id` of the previous\nturn and the new instruction. The history is maintained automatically if\n`store: true` was used.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\n// Turn 1: Initial generation (must use store: true)\nconst interaction1 = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  input: \"A claymation Newton\'s First Law stop motion video.\",\n  background: false,\n  store: true,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: { type: \'video\' }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\n// Turn 2: Edit (only pass the new instruction and reference the previous turn)\nconst interaction2 = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  previous_interaction_id: interaction1.id,\n  input: \"Now make it doodle style.\",\n  background: false,\n  store: true, // Keep storing if you want to continue the conversation\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: { type: \'video\' }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\nconst videoPart = interaction2.output_video;\n// ...\n```\n\n#### 6. Video Extension\n\nExtend an existing video by generating a seamless 3\342\200\22310 second continuation\n(`\'10s\'` default) at the tail end of the clip (up to 30s total length). Describe\nhow the scene should continue in your prompt (e.g., `\"Extend this video\"` or\n`\"Continue the scene: the camera pans across the mountains\"`).\n\nYou can extend:\n\n-   **Previously generated videos (multi-turn)**: Pass `previous_interaction_id`\n    from a prior interaction created with `store: true` (up to 10s per turn).\n-   **Uploaded videos**: Upload a video (`<= 10s`) via `ai.files.upload`, poll\n    `ai.files.get` until `state === \'ACTIVE\'`, and pass\n    `{ type: \'video\', uri: videoFile.uri }` in `input`.\n-   **With reference images**: Include up to 6 reference image(s) alongside the\n    video in `input` and describe in natural language how the character or\n    element in the reference image enters the extended scene (only reference\n    videos are restricted to new video generation, not video editing or\n    extension).\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n// ... initialization ...\n\n// Option A: Extend a previously generated video via multi-turn (requires store: true on Turn 1)\nconst extendedFromTurn = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  previous_interaction_id: interaction1.id,\n  input:\n    \'Continue the scene: the camera pulls back to reveal the entire workshop.\',\n  background: false,\n  store: true,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: {\n    type: \'video\',\n    duration: \'10s\', // \'3s\' to \'10s\' (\'10s\' default)\n  }\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\n// Option B: Extend an uploaded video (optionally guided by a reference image)\nlet baseVideo = await ai.files.upload({\n  file: \'my_video.mp4\',\n  config: { mimeType: \'video/mp4\' },\n});\nwhile (baseVideo.state === \'PROCESSING\') {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 10000));\n  baseVideo = await ai.files.get({ name: baseVideo.name || \'\' });\n}\nif (baseVideo.state === \'FAILED\') {\n  throw new Error(\'Video processing failed.\');\n}\n\nconst extendedFromUpload = await ai.interactions.create({\n  model: \'gemini-omni-1.2-flash\',\n  input: [\n    { type: \'video\', uri: baseVideo.uri },\n    // Optional reference image to introduce into the extended clip:\n    // { type: \'image\', mime_type: \'image/png\', data: characterBase64Bytes },\n    {\n      type: \'text\',\n      text: \'Continue the scene as the camera pans across the mountains.\',\n      // Or with reference image: \'Extend this video: have the character shown in the reference image enter the scene and wave.\'\n    },\n  ],\n  background: false,\n  store: false,\n  stream: false,\n  response_format: { type: \'video\' },\n}, { timeout: 300000 });\n\nconst extendedVideoPart = extendedFromUpload.output_video;\n// ...\n```\n"
