  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Interactions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on streamlining the interaction between components. Specifically, I\'m working on `/src/components/KamusModal.tsx` to accept an optional `initialQuery` prop and synchronize the `searchQuery` when the modal opens. This will improve the component\'s responsiveness. Additionally, I plan to modify `/src/views/LemariView.tsx` to accommodate the change.\n\n\n**Integrating Search Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the search functionality across the application. I\'ve wired `onOpenPanduan` in `/src/App.tsx` to `BerandaView`, and connected `kamusInitialQuery` and `lemariInitialSearch` to make the Hero Quick Search Bar in `BerandaView` work natively for both \"Kamus Istilah\" and \"Lemari Obat.\" I\'m also planning to enhance the chart card in `/src/components/RingkasanStokObatChart.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Hero View**\n\nI\'m now designing the hero view. I\'ve integrated a Hero Search Dock with quick buttons for \"Cari Kamus\" and \"Cari Lemari\", inspired by images 3 and 4. I\'ve added four Mountain Meadow Shortcut Tiles with crisp icons and a framed botanical illustration. The design includes a trust row with three pillars along the hero bottom, as well.\n\n\n**Developing Home Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now developing the home dashboard, specifically sections 02 and 03. I\'ve designed \"Cek Label Obat\" and \"Lemari Obat Saya\" cards with tooltips. I\'m building a 3-column insight row inspired by Image 1, featuring a scenario card, an editorial quote card with a botanical illustration, and a quick actions menu. I\'m also creating a 4-step DAGUSIBU flow and a home medication safety checklist with interactive checkboxes that persist locally.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "PrUBa9TKJpqsz7IP2O_eiQI"
